---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CashStar Pattern Library — Rob Pitt"
  description="How I set the modern standard for digital gift card purchase flows."
>
  <article class="case-study">
    <header class="case-study__header">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="case-study__meta">CashStar · 2014–2017 · Portland, ME</p>
        <h1 class="case-study__title">The pattern library that shaped how digital gift cards are bought.</h1>
        <p class="case-study__lede">
          I led the end-to-end redesign of CashStar's gift card platform and built the responsive pattern library that scaled across every retailer that white-labeled it — Best Buy, Nordstrom, Gap, Subway, and dozens more.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="case-study__label">The problem</p>
        <p>
          The existing gift card platform had accumulated years of tech debt. Poor conversion rates. No mobile optimization. Every retailer that white-labeled CashStar inherited the same UX pain, and no matter how good the marketing was, the checkout flow bled customers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section case-study__section--wide">
      <figure class="figure figure--split">
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/patterns/bestbuy-before.png" alt="Best Buy gift card flow — before redesign" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Before — the flow customers dropped out of.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/patterns/bestbuy-after.png" alt="Best Buy gift card flow — after redesign" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>After — the flow that shipped.</figcaption>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="case-study__label">My role</p>
        <p>
          I led the end-to-end redesign of the platform experience and built a responsive pattern library from scratch. Everything from motion behavior to input validation, in one system that other retailers could adopt without redoing the work.
        </p>

        <p class="case-study__label">Process</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Aligned on MVP and future requirements with product</li>
          <li>Usability studies on three prototypes to validate design direction</li>
          <li>Identified every screen and every flow across the buying journey</li>
          <li>Designed a fully annotated pattern library with reusable components</li>
          <li>Built interactions and animations to demonstrate intended behavior</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section case-study__section--wide">
      <figure class="figure">
        <img src="/case-studies/patterns/steps.gif" alt="Animated demonstration of the redesigned purchase flow steps" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>The redesigned steps in motion.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="case-study__label">The result</p>
        <p>
          The redesigned, mobile-optimized platform lifted <strong>conversion by 70%</strong> and cut <strong>purchase times in half</strong>. My pattern library became CashStar's scalable design system — the foundation every retailer built on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section case-study__section--wide">
      <figure class="figure">
        <img src="/case-studies/patterns/brands.gif" alt="Brands using the CashStar white-label platform" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>A slice of the brands that shipped on top of the system.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="case-study__label">What I actually did</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Resolved core UX pain points through user research</li>
          <li>Developed consistent, responsive patterns and components</li>
          <li>Dramatically improved customer experience metrics</li>
          <li>Set the foundation for efficient long-term design and development</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The modular system enabled every retailer that white-labeled CashStar to ship faster without cutting design corners. When people talk about "modern gift card UX," they're talking about a pattern I helped define.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="case-study__footer">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <a href="/#shipped" class="case-study__back">← back to all work</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @import "../../styles/case-study.css";
</style>
